The csrc/ directory contains unchanged CUDA and header files from vLLM
v0.32.0, commit 5df63a7203cdb9328d824a27b682e77c7b9928be:
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/tree/5df63a7203cdb9328d824a27b682e77c7b9928be/csrc

kernels.py retains unchanged Triton function definitions from that revision:
- vllm/models/deepseek_v4/common/ops/fused_indexer_q.py: _fp32x2_to_fp4x2
- vllm/models/deepseek_v41/common/ops/fused_compress_quant_cache.py:
  _rope_quant_insert_nvfp4_kernel

indexer.py carries _quantize_mxfp4_pair and the MXFP4 query kernel from
FusedIndexerQRopeMxFp4TritonKernel in fused_indexer_q.py, and
_indexer_k_norm_rope_quant_store_kernel from
vllm/models/deepseek_v41/common/ops/indexer_k_store.py at the same revision.
The query kernel is named _query_rope_quant_kernel outside its vLLM warmup
class; the function body is unchanged. Flare's wrapper supplies explicit
outputs and exposes the launches to complete-forward compilation.

candidates.py retains unchanged Triton definitions from
vllm/model_executor/kernels/attention/dsa/candidate_blocks.py and
sparse_mqa_logits.py at the same revision. They select blocks by maximum
score, expand/sort sparse block IDs, and remap selected columns to tokens.

LICENSE.vllm retains the Apache-2.0 license. The original source credits the
vLLM contributors; the CUDA source also identifies its TensorRT-LLM and vLLM
rotary-kernel inspirations. Flare supplies the isolated operator registration
and preparation build. It does not import the vLLM serving runtime.
